    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"xor (exclusive OR) is a bitwise operation referenced in the problem as the key operator in the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor stands for bitwise exclusive OR, a binary operation used in the problem to compare bits of two integers. It is the other key operator in the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor stands for bitwise exclusive OR, a binary operation used in the problem to compare bits of two integers. It is a key operator in the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"xor stands for bitwise exclusive OR, a binary operation used in the problem to compare bits of two integers. It is a core component of the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."</data>
