    <node id="&quot;MIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A variable in a programming context, likely representing a minimum value used in a mathematical expression to calculate an answer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A variable storing the minimum number of 0s (water cells) adjacent to the largest connected component of 1s found during BFS traversal."&lt;SEP&gt;"A variable storing the minimum number of boundary cells (0s) adjacent to the largest connected component(s)."&lt;SEP&gt;"MIN is a global variable storing the minimum number of surrounding 0s (cnt2) corresponding to the largest component of 1s, used for tie-breaking optimization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Min 是学生程序中用于存储最少敲碎灰色砖块数量的变量名，代表算法输出结果，是程序逻辑的核心输出目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"Min appears to be a variable or placeholder name used in a computational context, possibly representing a minimum value or a person's initials in an educational setting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-61548360973c5cefdc1038d32bf69e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43422d516179991d5c796063c71f443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4655c44a0c410e0c718d92b308d741b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e307f6e0f75e0c72f6c263b74efaa1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f24131db9a2e06f7a88e10188152d99d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A function named 'solve' that encapsulates the core logic for solving the '字符串外串' problem, called repeatedly for each test case in the student's program."&lt;SEP&gt;"A function that initializes the grid from input, runs BFS on all unvisited 1s, and outputs the minimum adjacent 0s for the largest component, serving as the main solution logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"solve 是学生程序中的核心函数，封装了读取输入、判断可行性、构造输出字符串的完整逻辑，是程序执行的主要事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"solve is a function in the student's program that computes a complex mathematical expression for the expected absolute difference between two uniformly random integers over given intervals, used as a subroutine for the main computation."&lt;SEP&gt;"solve is a function in the student's program that computes the expected absolute difference between two independent uniform random variables over given integer intervals."&lt;SEP&gt;"solve is a function called in the student program to process each test case, likely containing the core logic for answering the queries about permutation subinterval sorting and element position tracking."&lt;SEP&gt;"solve is a function in the student program that processes each test case, likely containing the logic to handle the permutation queries as described in the problem statement."&lt;SEP&gt;"solve is a function call in the student program that processes each test case, representing the core algorithmic task of answering the m queries about permutation element positions after sorting subintervals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f207867e95527d1c21eb90640d585ef3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be1dd97aefef7c188309086d2d51eecb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d353b59db67cab15706b3f74c4fa457&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2d77cdcffc291f16acc127cdfe41569&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8571d78ef0982dfe0d6ef86e585cbe98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
