      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"val(a) is the defined mathematical event or function representing the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, used to compute the expected value."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the defined value of the sequence, calculated as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements: Σ|a_{i-1} - a_i| for i from 2 to n, which is the quantity whose expectation is sought."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the defined value of a sequence, calculated as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements, which is the target quantity for which expectation is computed."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the defined value of the sequence, computed as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements; it is the central mathematical objective of the problem event."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is the mathematical function defined as the sum of absolute differences between consecutive elements in the sequence, which is the quantity whose expectation is being computed."</data>
