    <node id="&quot;TIC-TAC-TOE GAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tic-Tac-Toe Game is a 3x3 board game between 小L and 炸鸡, where the goal is to get three of one's marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is in a drawn state with equal moves made by both players, and it is now 小L's turn with a special one-time double-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based strategic game where two players, 小L and 炸鸡, take turns placing X and O marks, with the goal of forming three in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is in a drawn state with equal moves and 小L is to move next with a one-time double-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;The tic-tac-toe game is a 3x3 grid-based turn-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, where the objective is to be the first to align three of one’s own marks—either "X" or "O"—in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is currently in a drawn state, with both players having made an equal number of moves and no winner yet determined. Despite the board being filled to a point where neither side has achieved a winning line, the game remains unresolved because it is now 小L’s turn to move. 小L holds a special one-time privilege to make two moves in a single turn, a unique rule that alters the standard alternating-turn structure and introduces a strategic advantage. This double-move privilege is applicable only once during the game and is currently active, meaning 小L has the opportunity to influence the outcome by placing two marks in this turn, potentially creating a winning line or blocking 炸鸡’s future opportunities. The game’s status is therefore dynamic and pending 小L’s next action.&lt;SEP&gt;"The tic-tac-toe game is in a mid-game state with equal moves by both players, no winner yet, and it is now 小L's turn with a special rule allowing one double move."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'O' represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating the second player's symbol used to claim a cell in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O is the symbol used to denote a move made by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, representing the opponent's marker in the game state."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in a cell. It is one of the two symbolic states used to denote player ownership of a position."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, signifying the other player's pieces in the game state."&lt;SEP&gt;O is the symbol used to represent a move made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating ownership of a cell by 炸鸡 in the current game state. It is one of two player symbols (the other being X) used to track each player’s progress toward forming a winning line of three consecutive marks—horizontally, vertically, or diagonally. Each placement of O signifies one of 炸鸡’s chosen positions in the grid, contributing to their strategic effort to achieve a three-in-a-row and secure victory. As the opponent’s mark in the context of the game, O occupies one of the nine possible grid cells and is essential for determining the game’s state, outcomes, and potential winning configurations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8674c89c2bbd80ac2ed7bf4f4ece7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'G' represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet. It is a state marker used to denote unoccupied spaces in the game grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet. It is a state marker used in the game's grid representation."&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark yet; it is a state indicator within the game's grid system."&lt;SEP&gt;G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has yet placed a mark. It serves as a state indicator or state symbol within the game’s grid representation, used to denote unoccupied cells and to track the current game state. This marker is essential for determining valid next moves and analyzing the board’s configuration during gameplay. The symbol "G" stands for "Empty" or "Gap," and its consistent use across all descriptions confirms its role as a fundamental element in encoding the status of each cell in the tic-tac-toe grid, particularly in contexts involving game state recording and decision-making algorithms.&lt;SEP&gt;"G represents an empty cell on the 3x3 tic-tac-toe board, indicating a position where no player has placed a mark; it is a state marker in the game grid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41bb705f581ef523c90424ea77cfe827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64cb9d6867521174d17ba3213df66180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0414d324dc902fa7bfe392b580d12b0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a625df4ed1e048ecc8681beebcec0a9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fbf67613a3aed791c8801433f136cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e8674c89c2bbd80ac2ed7bf4f4ece7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031bf50845b77cce37dae6bb7e48b3a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3X3 BOARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 3x3 board is the playing field for the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j) where i and j range from 1 to 3, and each cell can contain 'X', 'O', or 'G' to denote player moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 board is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, where players place their marks to form a winning line."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 board is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, where players place their marks (X or O) to win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A row is a horizontal line of three cells in the 3x3 grid; a player wins by placing three of their marks in any single row."&lt;SEP&gt;"A row is a horizontal line of three cells on the 3x3 board; completing a row with three identical marks ('X' or 'O') results in a win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLUMN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A column is a vertical line of three cells in the 3x3 grid; a player wins by placing three of their marks in any single column."&lt;SEP&gt;"A column is a vertical line of three cells on the 3x3 board; completing a column with three identical marks ('X' or 'O') results in a win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAIN DIAGONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The main diagonal is the line of three cells from top-left to bottom-right (positions (1,1), (2,2), (3,3)) on the 3x3 board; completing this diagonal with identical marks results in a win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-DIAGONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The anti-diagonal is the line of three cells from top-right to bottom-left (positions (1,3), (2,2), (3,1)) on the 3x3 board; completing this diagonal with identical marks results in a win."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTRUCTOR OR EVALUATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An unnamed instructor or automated system that identified and recorded the student's incorrect answer and its deviation from the expected solution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1446a315ea545061645e2e34bdaaffae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 98-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An internal tracking identifier used by an educational or grading system to log and reference this specific error instance, implying an institutional framework for assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1446a315ea545061645e2e34bdaaffae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-02-08 15:18:42&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp associated with the error record, indicating the exact moment the error was logged in a system, functioning as a temporal landmark in an educational workflow."</data>
