    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERMUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A permutation is an array of length n containing each integer from 1 to n exactly once, forming the input data structure for all queries."&lt;SEP&gt;"A permutation is an array of n distinct integers from 1 to n, arranged in any order, forming the core data structure of the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"A permutation is an array of n distinct integers from 1 to n, each appearing exactly once, forming the core data structure manipulated in the problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4bbd9f3652366c894d3ef5e4694e35b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be1dd97aefef7c188309086d2d51eecb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBINTERVAL SORTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Subinterval sorting is the core operation in each query, where elements in range [l_i, r_i] are sorted in ascending order to determine the new location of the element originally at position c_i."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subinterval sorting is the operation of sorting elements within a specified range [l_i, r_i] of the permutation, which is the central computational task in each query."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be1dd97aefef7c188309086d2d51eecb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae03b8ab8904bfd565e3a28acd596fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELEMENT POSITION TRACKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Element position tracking refers to the process of determining where a specific element, originally at position c_i, moves after the subinterval [l_i, r_i] is sorted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be1dd97aefef7c188309086d2d51eecb</data>
    </node>
