    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;[RECORD ID: 3-1, TIMESTAMP: 2024-10-13 19:09:54]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program is the subject of this recorded evaluation event, which documents its incorrect output and failure to meet the problem requirements."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-4df85ce295d523e4b50f09ff04d5c7bc</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;ERROR DESCRIPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">300.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Student Program is the direct and primary subject of the Error Description, which systematically identifies it as fundamentally incorrect in its logic, output, and implementation. The Error Description evaluates the Student Program across multiple problem contexts, consistently flagging its outputs as incompatible with the required solution, particularly in relation to the specification of a “好矩阵” (good matrix). It documents critical logical flaws, including failures in median calculation, improper array partitioning, and incorrect handling of n-to-m transformations. The program is also found to fail in computing the true maximum and exhibits defective behavior in BFS state exploration, likely due to improper bounds (e.g., x ≤ 4 * m) and inadequate handling of edge cases. Despite the problem having a guaranteed correct solution, the Student Program’s implementation contains persistent and explicit deviations from the expected functionality, resulting in incorrect outputs under various input conditions. The Error Description notes that the Student Program achieves only partial correctness with a low score, indicating that while some components may function correctly, core logic defects prevent reliable, complete accuracy. These flaws are not isolated incidents but are consistently documented across evaluations, confirming that the Student Program is the central source of erroneous behavior. As a key diagnostic tool, the Error Description serves to explicitly link the program’s code to its identified failures, affirming that the Student Program is not merely suboptimal but fundamentally flawed in its design and execution.</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-47e1da39547e4d5d5cdafb2530c061c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f83dfef3345c73ed407093c9749130b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d177fa42f88e3250bf9921ff21987ec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504efc1d29aab22b90705499f57173fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4815d1a22ec8a935241a5f566cd9c42f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264071873a8220efc52cdb3c6f973f1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79af8c07e093eeaf2a8b54738698e7af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c02916b7b0e5a87f92d544844a99ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3eac5a8ba5cac7de40889ced9fb5315&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0b936b6b647a37d956fdf66cd57a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aa783b90d0126e6fe65518c125bef47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985dca88cf19334aa6bccf195ded5fbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc322d7318797c103f604c41177f547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f089790696661ee6abceff90f9924d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffc536726735c9911cd4a90d2ddb49f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0be1ff21d6f00384f294e712dc03c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb748d740807dc942d42a2dc4f25d05d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7638980c6db214619f264bda3c98a5b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e91156da41d8c127cfcd98fd99217c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8639879bd177c95139010b9025b24c97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72507ce11e78cbb0f5fe85180ed22a32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fa52e5b330629e1cee02304480f542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d2aa75d8324c591292a5206cbd69bde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de530eec1b33d2199269b22b88bb1c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d855de4fc3c8066acae7529422e672d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512301a13a22c9eae82f981e0542065a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5e545f02779dfb717361dfc31cb72c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a2665d10418a7ca4b53ae850057cff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad0b2a1773fb3f15dee0ac6d32877cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e9ce81e31f65b60ba40e243a8d1ba19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbb166f8ec0a1178f2d878ecaab5e98</data>
