      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"a_i is one of the two integers involved in the bitwise xor operation as required by the problem's condition."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-8b7bfa15e059051e591b4500f150f4b0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;A_J&quot;">
      <data key="d3">30.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"a_i and a_j are paired elements in the array for which the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j) must be evaluated."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i and a_j form a pair of elements in the array where i &lt; j, and their relationship is defined by the mathematical condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i and a_j are pairs of elements from the array where i &lt; j, and their relationship is defined by the condition a_i xor a_j = gcd(a_i, a_j)."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9bb8ae3fef264eb1654019ea7fdabc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54e2ed195b50756e6f2448b5f990c4b3</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;CNT[A[I]]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"cnt[a[i]] stores the frequency of each a_i value, enabling the algorithm to count multiple instances of the same number when computing valid pairs."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-91d5ad5a52520d2ee66b7e8855842a44</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;TOKITSUKAZE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Tokitsukaze defines the sequence elements a_i as random variables with bounded uniform distributions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze's problem centers on the random variables a_i, each drawn from [l_i, r_i], which form the sequence whose value is evaluated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tokitsukaze's problem revolves around the random generation of each a_i within given intervals, making a_i the fundamental variable of the problem."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;L_I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Each a_i is generated independently and uniformly from the interval defined by l_i and r_i, making l_i a direct constraint on the possible values of a_i."&lt;SEP&gt;"l_i sets the minimum possible value for a_i, directly constraining its random generation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;R_I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Each a_i is generated independently and uniformly from the interval defined by l_i and r_i, making r_i a direct constraint on the possible values of a_i."&lt;SEP&gt;"r_i sets the maximum possible value for a_i, directly constraining its random generation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;VAL(A)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">29.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Each a_i contributes to the computation of val(a) through its absolute difference with adjacent elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is computed directly from the consecutive pairs of a_i elements, making each a_i a critical component in determining the sequence's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"val(a) is directly computed from the sequence of a_i values through consecutive absolute differences, making each a_i a direct contributor to the value function."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-2a6cf2c1b884640bd458e20b236729e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;QUERY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The query function computes the expected absolute difference between a_{i} and a_{i-1} using their respective intervals [l_i, r_i] and [l_{i-1}, r_{i-1}], directly linking to the sequence elements."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-f8c9f94da5a947d7ca0394b058d44d06</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;L[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"L[i] defines the minimum possible value for a_i, constraining the uniform random distribution from which a_i is drawn."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A_I&quot;" target="&quot;R[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"R[i] defines the maximum possible value for a_i, working with L[i] to fully specify the random range for each sequence element."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-643a1dae351fde67dd0b6b4bafe4269b</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
