      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"G denotes empty cells within the 3x3 grid, indicating unoccupied positions available for play."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid contains cells marked 'G' to denote unoccupied positions available for future moves."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid contains 'G' symbols to denote unoccupied positions, which are critical for determining possible future moves."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid contains 'G' symbols in unoccupied cells, which represent available moves for either player during their turn."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'G' state indicates unoccupied cells within the 3x3 grid, representing available moves during gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"G marks indicate empty positions on the 3x3 grid, showing available spots for future moves."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'G' state indicates empty cells within the 3x3 grid, representing available positions for future moves."</data>
